Exception: the lettering on signs.
The glyph images crystalminer_{b52,c44,b34,b26,b17,r24,r20,r18,r16}_*
(and the lettering in the generated figures) are rendered from the DejaVu fonts, which are
derived from Bitstream Vera. See LICENSE.fonts for their licence, which must be kept with them.

The generated exhibit atom textures (crystalminer_atom_*.png) use the Jmol element-colour
convention; the colour values are factual data from ASE's jmol_colors table, not artwork.

Materials Project sample data: CC BY 4.0
----------------------------------------
The three baked crystal structures in data/mpcontribs/, and the files generated from them
(mods/crystalminer/exhibit_data.lua and tests/fixtures/exhibit_records.lua), are not covered by
the CC BY-SA licence above. They were fetched from the /structures/ endpoint of MPContribs, the
contribution platform of the Materials Project (https://materialsproject.org,
https://contribs.materialsproject.org):

    CaTiO3      structure 61ee26ff6b5f3ffa9e3b0d18
    SrTiO3      structure 602ec159388c44668e267444
    MgMn4O8-0   structure 5f1d4a5dea67c7d47f01af7c

The live exhibits fetch further structures from the same API while the game runs; each exhibit's
plaque names its Materials Project record and MPContribs as the source.

MPContribs publishes its public projects under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
(On 22 October 2026 the public MPContribs /projects/ listing gave the licence "CCA4", i.e.
CC BY 4.0, for all 72 projects, and the three structures above can be read without an API key.
The project each structure belongs to was not recorded when they were fetched.)

Credit: data from the Materials Project and its MPContribs platform. A. Jain et al., "The
Materials Project: A materials genome approach to accelerating materials innovation",
APL Materials 1, 011002 (2013).
